#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708686 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "feb75744-bff8-5944-a186-f92ae0bec582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708695}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708695} :answer-field/id #uuid "e70d4b7b-511c-5130-8cf5-49bbf69a63d5" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "70f19e9c-d33f-54b5-9ce6-3152c63e5129" :question/problem "![Directed segments: C_1: A to B; C_2: C to B; C_3: C to A](images/df/dff3182806adf9689792a2a8f3d048f0734637628aed2bd0622c382218821306.png)\n\nThe arrows show the orientations of the segments. The same continuous vector field $\\mathbf F$ is used throughout. The closed path $C$ follows $A\\to C\\to B\\to A$ **clockwise**. You are given\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=6\\\\\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-3\\\\\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the integral along $C_1$ in the direction of its arrows.\n\n$\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=$ {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Write $I_j=\\int_{C_j}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$ for each segment in its arrow direction. Compare each arrow with the requested traversal. Reversed segments contribute negative integrals. By additivity,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-I_1+I_2-I_3\\\\6&=-I_1+(-3)-(-3)\\\\6&=-I_1+0\\\\-I_1&=6\\\\I_1&=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final value is in the requested arrow direction."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708694 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc699aaa-27b0-5ca2-8e50-f9248fbd023b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708688}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708688} :answer-field/id #uuid "e765774b-567f-52e2-a8f1-9e297c56dd9a" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f93a7a1b-aa06-55f7-a30d-103abb369e90" :question/problem "![Directed segments: C_1: A to B; C_2: C to B; C_3: C to A](images/df/dff3182806adf9689792a2a8f3d048f0734637628aed2bd0622c382218821306.png)\n\nThe arrows show the orientations of the segments. The same continuous vector field $\\mathbf F$ is used throughout. The closed path $C$ follows $A\\to B\\to C\\to A$ **counterclockwise**. You are given\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=14\\\\\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=4\\\\\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the integral along $C_2$ in the direction of its arrows.\n\n$\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=$ {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Write $I_j=\\int_{C_j}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$ for each segment in its arrow direction. Compare each arrow with the requested traversal. Reversed segments contribute negative integrals. By additivity,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=I_1-I_2+I_3\\\\14&=(4)-I_2+(5)\\\\14&=-I_2+9\\\\-I_2&=5\\\\I_2&=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final value is in the requested arrow direction."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708717 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47ea32ee-92c4-5d00-8ea8-36c047ee9773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(4 y z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(3 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(- 5 x z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708730} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc39691-26e9-5969-bdb0-3aede86dd380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(- 4 y z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(3 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(5 x z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708733} {:answer/id #uuid "60c49f8a-ea2b-5d1e-bc9b-6247c8ca8eb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(- 3 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(- 4 y z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(- 5 x z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708734} {:answer/id #uuid "61c6c036-6f08-5b67-9200-4b2b2d557b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(- 3 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(4 y z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(- 5 x z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708735} {:answer/id #uuid "fe9072d0-f951-5acc-ba5c-dc1cceebbb82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(- 3 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(4 y z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(5 x z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708751}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708734} :answer-field/id #uuid "f50eae66-9fdd-509f-8bd1-ff9bb5faac05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "020ccb4a-0a5c-52f2-b92c-978cbd7a8029" :question/problem "Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=\\left(- 3 x y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(- 4 y z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(- 5 x z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}\n$$\n\nand let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth path in $\\mathbb{R}^{3}$. Which coordinate-integral expression is equivalent to $\\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}$?" :question/worked-solution "For a piecewise-smooth path and a field defined on it,\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_C \\left(P\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(Q\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(R\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z\n$$\n\nHere the whole coefficients, including their signs, are\n\n$$\nP=- 3 x y,\\quad Q=- 4 y z,\\quad R=- 5 x z\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the identity gives\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_C \\left(- 3 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(- 4 y z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(- 5 x z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708724 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "068746c4-42e2-5b8f-99ab-10c3878312f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(4 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(4 x z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(-3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708718} {:answer/id #uuid "1f30f583-4cc8-5bc3-9719-004c9b5e625d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(- 4 x z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(- 4 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708721} {:answer/id #uuid "3a20999b-6321-57fc-9484-3c84a4f15146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(4 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(-3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(4 x z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708726} {:answer/id #uuid "3c84e988-5684-5383-983e-bb2fe0c6b029" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(-3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(- 4 x z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(- 4 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708727} {:answer/id #uuid "ee93317b-e0f9-5ea4-b181-875f753f2b46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(4 x z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(4 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(-3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708748}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708718} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b2a973e-de3d-5bca-9678-e41c4a6cfa2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708732}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "36d4649e-eb21-5719-929a-e14c042d0ae7" :question/problem "Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=\\left(4 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(4 x z\\right)\\,\\mathb