$C$ be a piecewise-smooth path in $\\mathbb{R}^{3}$. Which coordinate-integral expression is equivalent to $\\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}$?" :question/worked-solution "For a piecewise-smooth path and a field defined on it,\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_C \\left(P\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(Q\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(R\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z\n$$\n\nHere the whole coefficients, including their signs, are\n\n$$\nP=5 x y,\\quad Q=4 y z,\\quad R=3 x z\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the identity gives\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_C \\left(5 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(4 y z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(3 x z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "537fe0c3-dcf2-5d90-98ac-eabf14818802" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/bf/bf2eaf93fa15b49f565a1cc2e3c9483dc1842cdfdccf1b992b6686d26a4a2fd2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708762} {:answer/id #uuid "5625bd67-e036-5e2f-955e-f24c3315d830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ca/cada4fcccd8fa8068d9511b707f6dd8cb64bc0e208b1a5a73879324217eccfde.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708763} {:answer/id #uuid "80c9173e-36b3-5a27-99e0-35a1a4b1cc96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/94/9458378a4920b27289a05b94d5865a3f3771d211275c9ede90395d3f23b2e579.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708768} {:answer/id #uuid "9ecd950c-d1d1-5c25-bb9c-021cd2aa139b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/38/38fad205b37d770a5e5ea1761549f3736ffaf44e640fa1d6565cdb9dc33d7002.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708773} {:answer/id #uuid "d685da93-f8b1-5748-81d1-f7991506e2b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ff/ff858ab9bc5d6aeaf99e495f9e3233be87d4cbe244239ac9d9b07bb7852aaf2e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708782}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708773} :answer-field/id #uuid "c24aeb71-5f5a-5f8a-b116-a42aa4e2297a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5f0af1f0-7afa-537c-b9e9-5a09af9f9d35" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)=- x + 2 y$ at the points $(-2,-2)$, $(2,0)$, $(-1,-2)$?\n\nEach orange dot marks the tail of an arrow. All diagrams use the same scale, with one grid square representing one unit in each direction. A blue ring around a dot denotes a zero vector." :question/worked-solution "The gradient is $\\nabla f=f_x\\mathbf{i}+f_y\\mathbf{j}$. Take the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(- x + 2 y\\right)=-1 \\\\ f_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(- x + 2 y\\right)=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y)=\\left(-1\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\left(2\\right)\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates of each starting point.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla f(-2,-2)&=\\langle -1,\\;2\\rangle=\\langle -1,\\;2\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(2,0)&=\\langle -1,\\;2\\rangle=\\langle -1,\\;2\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(-1,-2)&=\\langle -1,\\;2\\rangle=\\langle -1,\\;2\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the first component as horizontal displacement and the second as vertical displacement. Place each tail at its stated point and compare both direction and length. The matching diagram is:\n\n![](images/38/38fad205b37d770a5e5ea1761549f3736ffaf44e640fa1d6565cdb9dc33d7002.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708771 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0189902c-d68e-548f-8717-f6db5c50a7d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/93/93096406c8aa72a211ef14419e35065076e4ed4dcc314e4b117c35496111964c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708753} {:answer/id #uuid "154a803b-6d08-5d4e-b282-48f9966575eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/62/62a065aecbb0f24d13cc2acc8ce7752b30e6885fbfe88b6e869c771d12d504ce.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708755} {:answer/id #uuid "6a5d1cfe-568d-5b4f-aef8-290c0287027e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/60/609f714031faab39112024b4a099f421a694ab5e6d9c776de382b08696dec548.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708766} {:answer/id #uuid "b86feb84-3c53-5034-8b81-1dcef67c3396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/8f/8f0758216e36bb712ebc16936ef0152bdb0303506bf4f2cb140cf4731afdccf8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708777} {:answer/id #uuid "ce85ffe0-47e7-5544-836a-6bd009543bc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/f8/f87a50dc8269f9d29e864f00a098939f988ceb4e7548f15f4b4178e76f07cd18.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708780}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708753} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd3315a4-762f-53fd-aa33-972f90a86dc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "97a26e14-d1a1-56d8-a8a3-3dd1da2fe280" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)=2 x - y$ at the points $(1,-2)$, $(0,-1)$, $(2,-1)$?\n\nEach orange dot marks the tail of an arrow. All diagrams use the same scale, with one grid square representing one unit in each direction. A blue ring around a dot denotes a zero vector." :question/worked-solution "The gradient is $\\nabla f=f_x\\mathbf{i}+f_y\\mathbf{j}$. Take the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(2 x - y\\right)=2 \\\\ f_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(2 x - y\\right)=-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y)=\\left(2\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\left(-1\\right)\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates of each starting point.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla f(1,-2)&=\\langle 2,\\;-1\\rangle=\\langle 2,\\;-1\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(0,-1)&=\\langle 2,\\;-1\\rangle=\\langle 2,\\;-1\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(2,-1)&=\\langle 2,\\;-1\\rangle=\\langle 2,\\;-1\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the first component as horizontal displacement and the second as vertical displacement. Place each tail at its stated point and compare both direction and length. The matching diagram is:\n\n![](images/93/93096406c8aa72a211ef14419e35065076e4ed4dcc314e4b117c35496111964c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708781 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d0f4749-3c48-527e-8aa6-12318dae3ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/54/54ac6dc13ebcaa2547a396fd4ad0c7c94d0512e2fc2807ce6b2f626532879d78.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708759} {:answer/id #uuid "45547190-59d5-5f36-b2ff-4f92e443b0cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c5/c5365bfd95ad54e455d7d3ec66254ce7501c5030c971c751870cfa40ce5f9088.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708760} {:answer/id #uuid "8917d42c-165e-56be-b580-409135bc0575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/67/67d5820a4d0b29b06afe2ba84b4fea671a095a46bb598276c1baca03d6ddf1f7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708769} {:answer/id #uuid "9c8a978e-3cc5-571c-8f55-410a00f06bac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/2b/2b3d711b8443e4a71e9e94bbeadaa064a86c5242c471214e3afaf66424c8f569.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708772} {:answer/id #uuid "b84d1869-fbcc-59fe-bb92-96266b4c364b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/9a/9a9f006f84abc65ed7d7b1b54566bdbc5b486c3d9f2c8fd50573d4495d754da2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708776}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708772} :answer-field/id #uuid "688581b5-08e5-5ade-9324-1bce90b04f27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d4e87c95-faa1-579f-85aa-96319102596f" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)=- 2 x - y$ at the points $(-2,-1)$, $(0,-2)$, $(0,2)$?\n\nEach orange dot marks the tail of an arrow. All diagrams use the same scale, with one grid square representing one unit in each direction. A blue ring around a dot denotes a zero vector." :question/worked-solution "The gradient is $\\nabla f=f_x\\mathbf{i}+f_y\\mathbf{j}$. Take the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(- 2 x - y\\right)=-2 \\\\ f_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(- 2 x - y\\right)=-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y)=\\left(-2\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\left(-1\\right)\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates of each starting point.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla f(-2,-1)&=\\langle -2,\\;-1\\rangle=\\langle -2,\\;-1\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(0,-2)&=\\langle -2,\\;-1\\rangle=\\langle -2,\\;-1\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(0,2)&=\\langle -2,\\;-1\\rangle=\\langle -2,\\;-1\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the first component as horizontal displacement and the second as vertical displacement. Place each tail at its stated point and compare both direction and length. The matching diagram is:\n\n![](images/2b/2b3d711b8443e4a71e9e94bbeadaa064a86c5242c471214e3afaf66424c8f569.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708785 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0faa92b9-3ab5-56e2-bbcc-7c1c5226fb16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/18/1830e235f4e057d4b8f3cddfac6e5d000afea8466757b3688a8635c4f16b9c8a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708754} {:answer/id #uuid "1b5a75fd-3d14-5897-a4ac-4c4449322443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/a6/a6ebf9d64011a1960745f8ca64d5c5796e5caf938609c64e916171bbc110bd4f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708757} {:answer/id #uuid "750adb7c-d8fb-5c4f-91f5-4c8827931007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/f7/f777706df30234e4a1c11d707e7fc1d8612043ed1efc750848366550ac42a44d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708767} {:answer/id #uuid "a5637b66-5692-582f-9fe2-08cbd87347bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/f7/f7b241827063ba56301330faef3a5cbd183301e633a841cda063f668f13c18d0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708774} {:answer/id #uuid "e7edf2fa-c42e-586b-9ed6-486ecf89bb05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/a5/a5c07db07894365f5fbb24e32c18532c22e914755cc5bbe4827b550032b4cb37.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708786}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708757} :answer-field/id #uuid "45d22055-95c4-55d4-afdf-cb19f94772b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e4678783-cd1d-5c41-bd42-2be2eb88069f" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)=- 2 x + y$ at the points $(-1,0)$, $(0,0)$, $(-1,-2)$?\n\nEach orange dot marks the tail of an arrow. All diagrams use the same scale, with one grid square representing one unit in each direction. A blue ring around a dot denotes a zero vector." :question/worked-solution "The gradient is $\\nabla f=f_x\\mathbf{i}+f_y\\mathbf{j}$. Take the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(- 2 x + y\\right)=-2 \\\\ f_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(- 2 x + y\\right)=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y)=\\left(-2\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\left(1\\right)\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates of each starting point.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla f(-1,0)&=\\langle -2,\\;1\\rangle=\\langle -2,\\;1\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(0,0)&=\\langle -2,\\;1\\rangle=\\langle -2,\\;1\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(-1,-2)&=\\langle -2,\\;1\\rangle=\\langle -2,\\;1\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the first component as horizontal displacement and the second as vertical displacement. Place each tail at its stated point and compare both direction and length. The matching diagram is:\n\n![](images/a6/a6ebf9d64011a1960745f8ca64d5c5796e5caf938609c64e916171bbc110bd4f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "161beff8-b720-5d42-9ff5-f18b821446cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/3c/3ca68735b77e90ffcefbe3d143b57aad9486f8050bd2cac639dae106ea9bd9b3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708756} {:answer/id #uuid "3ac80284-7a63-5fa5-b71b-600c2b5c698b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/8b/8bf564196f43f6603ab1c27dd9ef99fd8438a06151990e8f050fac6441ad05a6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708758} {:answer/id #uuid "8b27d19e-82fc-59cb-9d3a-ad8d2e4958d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/43/437a782632be32d34c567c4489e089510f4476f8b66b227484740f720a305c72.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708770} {:answer/id #uuid "b1c302de-f0bb-5cb5-8335-b35187746284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/fe/fe7851cfc1de8e1c3a8ad4ce66a2931d5fb4c05ef1f398bf88cd34cd316e4360.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708775} {:answer/id #uuid "bf2e1a33-c2d0-5a92-9aeb-e9f6ea6d57a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/bc/bc6bc9c4aa7fd64b0ea280b0bb24c39dd8ef84ddb0ed3fdf7c321d5434395bb1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708778}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708775} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc89273b-b8f9-5a9a-a66e-b91922dd8235" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f4804001-6cce-53ea-ac39-643bd84dd039" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)=2 x - y$ at the points $(1,-1)$, $(2,0)$, $(2,-2)$?\n\nEach orange dot marks the tail of an arrow. All diagrams use the same scale, with one grid square representing one unit in each direction. A blue ring around a dot denotes a zero vector." :question/worked-solution "The gradient is $\\nabla f=f_x\\mathbf{i}+f_y\\mathbf{j}$. Take the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(2 x - y\\right)=2 \\\\ f_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(2 x - y\\right)=-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y)=\\left(2\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\left(-1\\right)\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates of each starting point.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla f(1,-1)&=\\langle 2,\\;-1\\rangle=\\langle 2,\\;-1\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(2,0)&=\\langle 2,\\;-1\\rangle=\\langle 2,\\;-1\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(2,-2)&=\\langle 2,\\;-1\\rangle=\\langle 2,\\;-1\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the first component as horizontal displacement and the second as vertical displacement. Place each tail at its stated point and compare both direction and length. The matching diagram is:\n\n![](images/fe/fe7851cfc1de8e1c3a8ad4ce66a2931d5fb4c05ef1f398bf88cd34cd316e4360.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708790 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4841d9df-ec05-5dd0-a702-9847da0168c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(2 e^{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(4 e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708792} {:answer/id #uuid "704b6d9e-c254-5497-96e7-19214185c677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(4 e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(- 2 e^{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708794} {:answer/id #uuid "879e37cc-8d39-5e42-abf3-439a630665fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(- 2 e^{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(- 4 e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708797} {:answer/id #uuid "8ea61edc-6fed-5058-ba8a-eab1f9b567e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(4 e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(2 e^{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708798} {:answer/id #uuid "e4d3fa95-8169-5576-b6a4-19c2541db786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(2 e^{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(- 4 e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708802}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708792} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac48a49c-4057-5b05-9cb7-ebaf322b04a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "27989807-7030-5006-8629-346a6ebdeeca" :question/problem "Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=\\left(2 e^{y}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(4 e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\nand let $C$ be parametrized by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\left\\langle t,3 t^{2} - 1\\right\\rangle,\\quad 0\\leq t\\leq 1.\n$$ Which coordinate-integral expression is equivalent to $\\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}$?" :question/worked-solution "For a piecewise-smooth path and a field defined on it,\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_C \\left(P\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(Q\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nHere the whole coefficients, including their signs, are\n\n$$\nP=2 e^{y},\\quad Q=4 e^{x}\n$$\n\nThe parametrization is not needed to express the integral using coordinate differentials.\n\nSubstituting into the identity gives\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_C \\left(2 e^{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(4 e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708793 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0769b8f4-443c-5d29-8bd3-4199ba1a12ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(4 e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(- 3 e^{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708789} {:answer/id #uuid "3da7c332-9a25-5049-b21b-646e185d14e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(3 e^{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(- 4 e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708791} {:answer/id #uuid "7a5eb3b6-d8cd-5058-9d44-a111bc80e980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(4 e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(3 e^{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708795} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a76bb1-8b18-58e1-8ef7-cc130f5e083f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(- 3 e^{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(- 4 e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708800} {:answer/id #uuid "ba85844b-8420-5945-a436-ac447aa8d627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_C \\left(- 3 e^{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(4 e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708801}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708801} :answer-field/id #uuid "82287b26-cbfb-5165-a585-0b657765631a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5b147ae0-f606-50bb-8d3f-84f69cd48563" :question/problem "Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=\\left(- 3 e^{y}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(4 e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\nand let $C$ be parametrized by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\left\\langle t,t^{2} + 2\\right\\rangle,\\quad 0\\leq t\\leq 1.\n$$ Which coordinate-integral expression is equivalent to $\\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}$?" :question/worked-solution "For a piecewise-smooth path and a field defined on it,\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_C \\left(P\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(Q\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nHere the whole coefficients, including their signs, are\n\n$$\nP=- 3 e^{y},\\quad Q=4 e^{x}\n$$\n\nThe parametrization is not needed to express the integral using coordinate differentials.\n\nSubstituting into the identity gives\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_C \\left(- 3 e^{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(4 e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20cc6aa3-1a8d-5b23-8610-118dbc104ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- 5 x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(3 z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708803} {:answer/id #uuid "9e453191-96dc-5d28-bdac-c74714eed31a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(5 x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(3 z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708806} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8d338c-a21e-57e1-a30e-db4509aacbc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- 3 z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(5 x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708807} {:answer/id #uuid "e8dd3fcb-62ff-5322-a216-1ce2ed522519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(3 z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(5 x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708808} {:answer/id #uuid "f59ce545-33af-57c9-a431-628e8c683226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(- 5 x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(- 3 z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708809}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708806} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e46f185-3451-5b52-8587-4cfcce94ec34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708805}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "29fee7ae-c5cc-5cbd-bbce-6748047161a0" :question/problem "Match the coefficients of the coordinate differentials in\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(2 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(5 x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(3 z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z\n$$\n\nwith the components of a vector field. Which field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)$ gives this coordinate representation of $\\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}$?" :question/worked-solution "For a piecewise-smooth path and a field defined on it,\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_C \\left(P\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(Q\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(R\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z\n$$\n\nHere the whole coefficients, including their signs, are\n\n$$\nP=2 y,\\quad Q=5 x^{2},\\quad R=3 z\n$$\n\nPlace those coefficients on the corresponding basis vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)&=\\left(2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(5 x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(3 z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}\\\\ \\int_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}&=\\int_C \\left(2 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(5 x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y+\\left(3 z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708813 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b0c81dc-1a95-5aa1-aba6-5f6434124280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/57/57708ff6e0f7e8aef80fdbcb851028af178a9f2d2226e43339a7aa844a292d9f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708810} {:answer/id #uuid "4692e019-77a7-54f0-993e-b89d7073834d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/b4/b4d231c7b3cc44fee29b4055d0e2851160c9b774b984e614a7d8c2e550999572.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708815} {:answer/id #uuid "baf0ce7f-f418-5ffe-aec1-f4afcd183fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/73/73e40361e7974deab7b4b01f14d08dd6f69f27a1aa89b2327d0538f8ad68b5fa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708827} {:answer/id #uuid "d0cb46ef-0dd2-53e6-b0c5-6181b229d531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/5e/5e06a96a8d41090644414658adde8fa74cfc441ba5c31076838cbf676973abd6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708828} {:answer/id #uuid "d116fe3c-5043-59e0-91fc-4ca5968bf0dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/21/216eb04c210df719881530b02def8f660951ffc598cdee759b88273b3faf09e9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708829}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708815} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4a70717-3544-5098-a569-da22adeb20ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1f703a9e-e9cf-543b-a638-c058386b6717" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)=\\left(\\frac{\\left(- x - y\\right)^2}{2}\\right)$ at the points $(2,-2)$, $(-1,-1)$, $(0,0)$?\n\nEach orange dot marks the tail of an arrow. All diagrams use the same scale, with one grid square representing one unit in each direction. A blue ring around a dot denotes a zero vector." :question/worked-solution "The gradient is $\\nabla f=f_x\\mathbf{i}+f_y\\mathbf{j}$. Take the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(- x - y\\right)^2}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=1\\cdot\\left(- x - y\\right)\\cdot(-1)=-\\left(- x - y\\right) \\\\ f_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(- x - y\\right)^2}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=1\\cdot\\left(- x - y\\right)\\cdot(-1)=-\\left(- x - y\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y)=\\left(-\\left(- x - y\\right)\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\left(-\\left(- x - y\\right)\\right)\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nFor substitution, write $t(x,y)=- x - y$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nt(2,-2)&=(-1)(2)+(-1)(-2)=0 \\\\ \\nabla f(2,-2)&=\\langle (-1)(0),\\;(-1)(0)\\rangle=\\langle 0,\\;0\\rangle \\\\ t(-1,-1)&=(-1)(-1)+(-1)(-1)=2 \\\\ \\nabla f(-1,-1)&=\\langle (-1)(2),\\;(-1)(2)\\rangle=\\langle -2,\\;-2\\rangle \\\\ t(0,0)&=(-1)(0)+(-1)(0)=0 \\\\ \\nabla f(0,0)&=\\langle (-1)(0),\\;(-1)(0)\\rangle=\\langle 0,\\;0\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the first component as horizontal displacement and the second as vertical displacement. Place each tail at its stated point and compare both direction and length. The matching diagram is:\n\n![](images/b4/b4d231c7b3cc44fee29b4055d0e2851160c9b774b984e614a7d8c2e550999572.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708814 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b3e4a15-046b-5f90-84c8-dcaac1496654" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d0/d01d806e662fbd4440b8a71755e0d7e438bf81c160889953e787f6799e7fcfe2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708816} {:answer/id #uuid "a344d00f-70e7-5f92-a92b-7d30f13c5530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/a8/a8c46d823edf8d1e9602f6bc82ac8b0b6e399243f43eabe1be1eb3b7cacddd73.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708823} {:answer/id #uuid "da9e075d-c5e2-56d7-825f-e35877959136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d4/d43da9f0f99380317f33f3b74f30f9fd1d0d6a1d28562c1bec34daa6c66c303c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708830} {:answer/id #uuid "e9fe174f-806d-5358-a34a-056e684c8956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/03/03f583ea9f2ccf4c36270a9676091a3ccc80c2b78164902729da2e702b0771df.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708833} {:answer/id #uuid "f4064c03-49cf-5d17-af9f-3068012bc1e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/38/38c542fe44c457b7bfe85a0f49c7237e6a735c9dad5c07d409f82a39e3123f59.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708836}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708816} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3066874-8cd8-5610-b0b2-21915375157e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "43c765db-6918-5457-80fb-3ec703b07de9" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)=-\\left(\\frac{\\left(- 2 x - 2 y\\right)^2}{2}\\right)$ at the points $(-1,1)$, $(-2,1)$, $(0,-1)$?\n\nEach orange dot marks the tail of an arrow. All diagrams use the same scale, with one grid square representing one unit in each direction. A blue ring around a dot denotes a zero vector." :question/worked-solution "The gradient is $\\nabla f=f_x\\mathbf{i}+f_y\\mathbf{j}$. Take the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(-\\left(\\frac{\\left(- 2 x - 2 y\\right)^2}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=-1\\cdot\\left(- 2 x - 2 y\\right)\\cdot(-2)=2\\left(- 2 x - 2 y\\right) \\\\ f_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(-\\left(\\frac{\\left(- 2 x - 2 y\\right)^2}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=-1\\cdot\\left(- 2 x - 2 y\\right)\\cdot(-2)=2\\left(- 2 x - 2 y\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y)=\\left(2\\left(- 2 x - 2 y\\right)\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\left(2\\left(- 2 x - 2 y\\right)\\right)\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nFor substitution, write $t(x,y)=- 2 x - 2 y$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nt(-1,1)&=(-2)(-1)+(-2)(1)=0 \\\\ \\nabla f(-1,1)&=\\langle (2)(0),\\;(2)(0)\\rangle=\\langle 0,\\;0\\rangle \\\\ t(-2,1)&=(-2)(-2)+(-2)(1)=2 \\\\ \\nabla f(-2,1)&=\\langle (2)(2),\\;(2)(2)\\rangle=\\langle 4,\\;4\\rangle \\\\ t(0,-1)&=(-2)(0)+(-2)(-1)=2 \\\\ \\nabla f(0,-1)&=\\langle (2)(2),\\;(2)(2)\\rangle=\\langle 4,\\;4\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the first component as horizontal displacement and the second as vertical displacement. Place each tail at its stated point and compare both direction and length. The matching diagram is:\n\n![](images/d0/d01d806e662fbd4440b8a71755e0d7e438bf81c160889953e787f6799e7fcfe2.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708834 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "101d05cb-c1ab-53d6-b154-6e8b3aac0742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/55/55944b4b37b8da336e75a22908ab096c9092922502261eb9e5ffd298f6e4cea3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708811} {:answer/id #uuid "18ca9a9b-6b25-52cf-bf92-a5ae18aa0fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/b8/b86b6521bbcdc981e9abb471a3abc4eed22a2f8e7d66c4d6e43970cddd9e664f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708812} {:answer/id #uuid "7c438055-b7ef-519b-9ad0-2a2dc9849251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/cb/cb505d5ea716ad0f5ac3516033b0f1c3e289d571c8720631ace566247749bd44.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708819} {:answer/id #uuid "8d09dd1a-0396-5e15-8044-c77f6f694102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/95/951a46e1af239bd71e086bd83c564e23716625bb726b92d1d1e6c665e1580efd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708820} {:answer/id #uuid "e9a48ea7-5149-59e1-948b-c914aebb65ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/b8/b838d85c088ccff99b93f8eb78cc257910db6b581840534692521bc46d11802d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708832}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708811} :answer-field/id #uuid "b78d5121-376d-50f3-beab-b7046e94624a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ed6fcd3c-fb2f-57f2-b74d-674302be47fd" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)=\\left(\\frac{\\left(x - y\\right)^2}{2}\\right)$ at the points $(2,0)$, $(0,1)$, $(-1,-2)$?\n\nEach orange dot marks the tail of an arrow. All diagrams use the same scale, with one grid square representing one unit in each direction. A blue ring around a dot denotes a zero vector." :question/worked-solution "The gradient is $\\nabla f=f_x\\mathbf{i}+f_y\\mathbf{j}$. Take the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(x - y\\right)^2}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=1\\cdot\\left(x - y\\right)\\cdot(1)=\\left(x - y\\right) \\\\ f_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(x - y\\right)^2}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=1\\cdot\\left(x - y\\right)\\cdot(-1)=-\\left(x - y\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y)=\\left(\\left(x - y\\right)\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\left(-\\left(x - y\\right)\\right)\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nFor substitution, write $t(x,y)=x - y$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nt(2,0)&=(1)(2)+(-1)(0)=2 \\\\ \\nabla f(2,0)&=\\langle (1)(2),\\;(-1)(2)\\rangle=\\langle 2,\\;-2\\rangle \\\\ t(0,1)&=(1)(0)+(-1)(1)=-1 \\\\ \\nabla f(0,1)&=\\langle (1)(-1),\\;(-1)(-1)\\rangle=\\langle -1,\\;1\\rangle \\\\ t(-1,-2)&=(1)(-1)+(-1)(-2)=1 \\\\ \\nabla f(-1,-2)&=\\langle (1)(1),\\;(-1)(1)\\rangle=\\langle 1,\\;-1\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the first component as horizontal displacement and the second as vertical displacement. Place each tail at its stated point and compare both direction and length. The matching diagram is:\n\n![](images/55/55944b4b37b8da336e75a22908ab096c9092922502261eb9e5ffd298f6e4cea3.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708835 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e39b060-1f81-503d-83a0-7c2755209511" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/89/898938c1a4374e80f62a8aa3d8d13680b74cbe5763514f51f16acebdb8c8e2f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708817} {:answer/id #uuid "7a807efe-ffe3-5015-97e5-57a73a322df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/14/149163a58cc8080096d38eab543f77c5b3e732de8b089843046a4f450eada599.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708818} {:answer/id #uuid "8f90121d-e079-5976-a2ce-0a934a950d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/48/4802146a9966405af67a60e6bf079660081378e2613b8cf7f6e21486abbeb016.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708821} {:answer/id #uuid "b091f4a2-d51c-5381-a621-5441296c44a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/80/80fb364f63276ca3c7467a130716db5ff508ce0abea1907ce96ed7199029af37.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708824} {:answer/id #uuid "e432620a-ab0a-556c-86fc-1eaa56b59f0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/47/4787df14c8a57874794f857330d3e18ae583b5ecedd3470da8246bb4f1cfde43.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708831}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708818} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8f8b78c-cd1d-54fc-a875-ce4bfe0439bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ee942509-d654-59a2-8a72-c9583280ee35" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)=-\\left(\\frac{\\left(- x - y\\right)^2}{2}\\right)$ at the points $(0,1)$, $(-2,0)$, $(0,-1)$?\n\nEach orange dot marks the tail of an arrow. All diagrams use the same scale, with one grid square representing one unit in each direction. A blue ring around a dot denotes a zero vector." :question/worked-solution "The gradient is $\\nabla f=f_x\\mathbf{i}+f_y\\mathbf{j}$. Take the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(-\\left(\\frac{\\left(- x - y\\right)^2}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=-1\\cdot\\left(- x - y\\right)\\cdot(-1)=\\left(- x - y\\right) \\\\ f_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(-\\left(\\frac{\\left(- x - y\\right)^2}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=-1\\cdot\\left(- x - y\\right)\\cdot(-1)=\\left(- x - y\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y)=\\left(\\left(- x - y\\right)\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\left(\\left(- x - y\\right)\\right)\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nFor substitution, write $t(x,y)=- x - y$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nt(0,1)&=(-1)(0)+(-1)(1)=-1 \\\\ \\nabla f(0,1)&=\\langle (1)(-1),\\;(1)(-1)\\rangle=\\langle -1,\\;-1\\rangle \\\\ t(-2,0)&=(-1)(-2)+(-1)(0)=2 \\\\ \\nabla f(-2,0)&=\\langle (1)(2),\\;(1)(2)\\rangle=\\langle 2,\\;2\\rangle \\\\ t(0,-1)&=(-1)(0)+(-1)(-1)=1 \\\\ \\nabla f(0,-1)&=\\langle (1)(1),\\;(1)(1)\\rangle=\\langle 1,\\;1\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the first component as horizontal displacement and the second as vertical displacement. Place each tail at its stated point and compare both direction and length. The matching diagram is:\n\n![](images/14/149163a58cc8080096d38eab543f77c5b3e732de8b089843046a4f450eada599.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "468e8427-1215-5f16-9e5a-ad1469350852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/4a/4ae72fa42b5e3ff52805d22979952eeb9c77d03f5df7a2948fe1096ccb01e9d2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708845} {:answer/id #uuid "481982ad-4226-5f2f-a15a-5e6b6fc0b39b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c0/c0356769b45e0fd459579dd6d559cafc672c406cb0f236c7ba6740eea6ee683f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708846} {:answer/id #uuid "8432e7c4-cdb9-58c2-b192-1b89a0d73632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/29/29bf0b5ad574318954ccf4bdee1b429b40ed39204fdbacebf21da27cb6efce3f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708855} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc1a1be-811a-5d4b-922b-c5d4adf64454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/e6/e628d4db5c1aa54819d8893f3fb32682f3931eb5eb57de57adbd30f996d51d6a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708859} {:answer/id #uuid "e767967f-6a83-54e5-993e-9ebbaabd0b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c6/c638ec05719029ee3b770cd52e09bf33cf3010eeeaf558160ca9ac1ae5d7130c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708862}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708862} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cc4af27-d419-587d-af7b-9d8c6108198c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3ff32acb-e9c6-5eef-8fa8-1530423b9d0d" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)=- x^{2} + \\frac{y^{2}}{2}$ at the points $(-2,-1)$, $(-1,1)$, $(0,1)$?\n\nEach orange dot marks the tail of an arrow. All diagrams use the same scale, with one grid square representing one unit in each direction. A blue ring around a dot denotes a zero vector." :question/worked-solution "The gradient is $\\nabla f=f_x\\mathbf{i}+f_y\\mathbf{j}$. Take the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(- x^{2} + \\frac{y^{2}}{2}\\right)=- 2 x \\\\ f_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(- x^{2} + \\frac{y^{2}}{2}\\right)=y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y)=\\left(- 2 x\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\left(y\\right)\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates of each starting point.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla f(-2,-1)&=\\langle (-2)(-2),\\;(1)(-1)\\rangle=\\langle 4,\\;-1\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(-1,1)&=\\langle (-2)(-1),\\;(1)(1)\\rangle=\\langle 2,\\;1\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(0,1)&=\\langle (-2)(0),\\;(1)(1)\\rangle=\\langle 0,\\;1\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the first component as horizontal displacement and the second as vertical displacement. Place each tail at its stated point and compare both direction and length. The matching diagram is:\n\n![](images/c6/c638ec05719029ee3b770cd52e09bf33cf3010eeeaf558160ca9ac1ae5d7130c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708848 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b55922c-6d41-5d49-81b3-c79fc0721cb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/61/6166072093c28085cdc8d3d2ff010efdaad44f95d87c06820efa7a97bd6980a8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708839} {:answer/id #uuid "60852eb1-5711-5641-be43-47ee97a1df6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c5/c585d66373e244ec9b8fbc574cf8d2b955fa07896574e751b76b5e12cc63c03e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708850} {:answer/id #uuid "7e9f879a-0a11-52d7-a5d7-e63ad729d8e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/5e/5eb0ae0d8f19521f7b249ecc0379d56d7e781a4cb9275b2bdab9d86542a559b6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708853} {:answer/id #uuid "caa4223d-977f-547f-9539-8c2a63829b2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/03/03a20503d16ca1e69e009ab6a6e5d20c09f714784965b19f2740cdd2615b79b3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708860} {:answer/id #uuid "feac3edc-a3f3-55ae-86b1-f551c4bb3c65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/b8/b8d6ab4c4433c735859b0821cc3f2b4699b0f162f6a0a416b882384fada58554.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708865}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708850} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9c8e90f-6223-5fe6-b4e7-de3c1fc44b28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5071a6d4-cf94-5d29-b5dd-370f93feae40" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)=\\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{y^{2}}{2}$ at the points $(-1,-1)$, $(2,0)$, $(-2,2)$?\n\nEach orange dot marks the tail of an arrow. All diagrams use the same scale, with one grid square representing one unit in each direction. A blue ring around a dot denotes a zero vector." :question/worked-solution "The gradient is $\\nabla f=f_x\\mathbf{i}+f_y\\mathbf{j}$. Take the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(\\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{y^{2}}{2}\\right)=x \\\\ f_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(\\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{y^{2}}{2}\\right)=y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y)=\\left(x\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\left(y\\right)\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates of each starting point.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla f(-1,-1)&=\\langle (1)(-1),\\;(1)(-1)\\rangle=\\langle -1,\\;-1\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(2,0)&=\\langle (1)(2),\\;(1)(0)\\rangle=\\langle 2,\\;0\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(-2,2)&=\\langle (1)(-2),\\;(1)(2)\\rangle=\\langle -2,\\;2\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the first component as horizontal displacement and the second as vertical displacement. Place each tail at its stated point and compare both direction and length. The matching diagram is:\n\n![](images/c5/c585d66373e244ec9b8fbc574cf8d2b955fa07896574e751b76b5e12cc63c03e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "261a3cc6-9a19-53d2-a1d3-05a4a0954c20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/7a/7ab6035f70fa877043638a5fa448189e028daf2baad676856f62926c8b7386fc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708840} {:answer/id #uuid "461962ae-519c-508e-a93a-6443ab1c0ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/9b/9b6e0ed6a6fe35c9710580b04ed523f1b79fa556346ed41c2ea7435068ec4633.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708844} {:answer/id #uuid "5283b4d6-c674-57ab-b90b-fdc78d6fc3bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ac/acb4484d4d03358a101f783548821b05b0dbd8ce1795cfa94787a323e5df29f7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708849} {:answer/id #uuid "654c18e8-8824-534e-9025-3f5d31589b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d1/d16fd9499c21e23703a2bcaa4e5355ebc15ffc01ad9630f1d8a710ba0a4462ce.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708851} {:answer/id #uuid "8331f804-49c0-513e-bdff-5194853e39b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/22/225d619f1f62192e542b42a65f9104a9001fd9bfbfa37a4f654cfb6057f026dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708854}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708844} :answer-field/id #uuid "09bc5c22-1173-572d-bba8-3ae587ed3563" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7cd1cd0f-57cf-5b32-b4eb-2cba805e43c3" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)=\\frac{x^{2}}{2} - y^{2}$ at the points $(-1,2)$, $(1,0)$, $(0,-2)$?\n\nEach orange dot marks the tail of an arrow. All diagrams use the same scale, with one grid square representing one unit in each direction. A blue ring around a dot denotes a zero vector." :question/worked-solution "The gradient is $\\nabla f=f_x\\mathbf{i}+f_y\\mathbf{j}$. Take the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(\\frac{x^{2}}{2} - y^{2}\\right)=x \\\\ f_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(\\frac{x^{2}}{2} - y^{2}\\right)=- 2 y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y)=\\left(x\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\left(- 2 y\\right)\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates of each starting point.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla f(-1,2)&=\\langle (1)(-1),\\;(-2)(2)\\rangle=\\langle -1,\\;-4\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(1,0)&=\\langle (1)(1),\\;(-2)(0)\\rangle=\\langle 1,\\;0\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(0,-2)&=\\langle (1)(0),\\;(-2)(-2)\\rangle=\\langle 0,\\;4\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the first component as horizontal displacement and the second as vertical displacement. Place each tail at its stated point and compare both direction and length. The matching diagram is:\n\n![](images/9b/9b6e0ed6a6fe35c9710580b04ed523f1b79fa556346ed41c2ea7435068ec4633.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2958eeb6-dcfd-590d-be40-67044cfc98d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/cf/cfcd62448cbd1f94e456d857967313c7a05425e34b9f563f4c16ecf412a3b3f0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708841} {:answer/id #uuid "35c9bbcf-67d2-5c52-9c45-1658cee2cf1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/4e/4e7146d47fd92699ed69c96295c2fa1070cf08638047e40ff781b15689564504.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708842} {:answer/id #uuid "a6be5f65-2dec-5438-93c3-381afbd2c9c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/2f/2fac50d3e29c6d576e68ad45dff033824bfbf4435e0ac634c6d90bea140584eb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708857} {:answer/id #uuid "bdceb577-2b24-5dc3-b462-c452ca480dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d4/d486cbddb1260ba830cd11e5bb5b7ef0e1fd0bde1e4eb8bac6c52c13b7fceec4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708858} {:answer/id #uuid "ebba4dbe-abc8-56e7-a35b-de08123e1952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c0/c06df1c49a0325eba3f0b5bca2b66cb701bfeddd3338365203effeda5ad1e82a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708863}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708841} :answer-field/id #uuid "e55bffcb-43cc-5f93-89ec-dc06e2d26826" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "974b29d3-2cbd-57ca-892b-26d86466912e" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)=- x^{2} + y^{2}$ at the points $(-1,-2)$, $(2,-1)$, $(1,0)$?\n\nEach orange dot marks the tail of an arrow. All diagrams use the same scale, with one grid square representing one unit in each direction. A blue ring around a dot denotes a zero vector." :question/worked-solution "The gradient is $\\nabla f=f_x\\mathbf{i}+f_y\\mathbf{j}$. Take the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(- x^{2} + y^{2}\\right)=- 2 x \\\\ f_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(- x^{2} + y^{2}\\right)=2 y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y)=\\left(- 2 x\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\left(2 y\\right)\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates of each starting point.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla f(-1,-2)&=\\langle (-2)(-1),\\;(2)(-2)\\rangle=\\langle 2,\\;-4\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(2,-1)&=\\langle (-2)(2),\\;(2)(-1)\\rangle=\\langle -4,\\;-2\\rangle \\\\ \\nabla f(1,0)&=\\langle (-2)(1),\\;(2)(0)\\rangle=\\langle -2,\\;0\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the first component as horizontal displacement and the second as vertical displacement. Place each tail at its stated point and compare both direction and length. The matching diagram is:\n\n![](images/cf/cfcd62448cbd1f94e456d857967313c7a05425e34b9f563f4c16ecf412a3b3f0.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708885 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10730773-f182-547e-89ad-1a06f94938e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708883} {:answer/id #uuid "10e9ed1c-0c5d-5a1a-a9af-e2ee5cde128e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{19\\sqrt5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708884} {:answer/id #uuid "335ab0ef-e877-5eae-9f71-d56d1b14947f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708890} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e10f04-dfbb-5892-8258-9b071bb583e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708899} {:answer/id #uuid "f804eabe-c621-5027-a098-1b1ed7fd54de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\sqrt5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708903}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708884} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bcda38c-478a-50c8-a88c-9cdc6542969b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708896}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1420a100-b3ff-5c74-bbc0-4e8d6cf5d35d" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int_C xy\\,\\mathrm{d}s$, where $C$ is the line segment from $(1,1)$ to $(3,2)$." :question/worked-solution "Use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nWith $\\mathbf a=(1,1)$ and $\\mathbf b=(3,2)$, a parametrization is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\mathbf a+t(\\mathbf b-\\mathbf a)=(1+2t,1+t),\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n$$\n\nIts endpoints are $\\mathbf r(0)=(1,1)$ and $\\mathbf r(1)=(3,2)$. Computing the derivative and speed gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r'(t)=(2,1),\\qquad \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|=\\sqrt{2^2+1^2}=\\sqrt5.\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates and expand their product:\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=(1+2t)(1+t)=1+3t+2t^2.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C xy\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n&=\\sqrt5\\int_0^1(1+3t+2t^2)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\sqrt5\\left[t+\\frac32t^2+\\frac23t^3\\right]_0^1\\\\\n&=\\sqrt5\\left(1+\\frac32+\\frac23\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{19\\sqrt5}{6}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708898 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27d088f6-54d8-5f2e-8d3b-5f1b9c931c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^2-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708888} {:answer/id #uuid "308eec89-6bc9-5b3f-8266-2514b269e016" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt2e^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708889} {:answer/id #uuid "3a80398b-aeac-5628-ba55-ec46e899f545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt2(e^2-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708891} {:answer/id #uuid "6cca29d8-3935-5b14-8e89-4d75937a74c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt2(e^2-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708893} {:answer/id #uuid "ed4b559e-3498-5f50-aa18-368ef5975c8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt2(e-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708902}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708891} :answer-field/id #uuid "92ed8755-2a8f-5d69-adf7-de01ec8d61fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c9548aa8-5c38-5823-941a-a66688efa9df" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int_C (2x+1)e^{xy}\\,\\mathrm{d}s$, where $C$ is the line segment from $(0,1)$ to $(1,2)$." :question/worked-solution "Use the scalar line-integral formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor $\\mathbf a=(0,1)$ and $\\mathbf b=(1,2)$, take\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\mathbf a+t(\\mathbf b-\\mathbf a)=(t,1+t),\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n$$\n\nThe endpoint check gives $\\mathbf r(0)=(0,1)$ and $\\mathbf r(1)=(1,2)$. Also,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r'(t)=(1,1),\\qquad \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|=\\sqrt{1^2+1^2}=\\sqrt2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting both coordinates gives\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=(2t+1)e^{t(1+t)}=(2t+1)e^{t+t^2}.\n$$\n\nThus the required integral becomes\n\n$$\n\\sqrt2\\int_0^1(2t+1)e^{t+t^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of the exponent is $1+2t$, which matches the factor outside the exponential. Set $u=t+t^2$, so $\\mathrm{d}u=(1+2t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t$. The bounds change from $t=0,1$ to $u=0,2$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C(2x+1)e^{xy}\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n&=\\sqrt2\\int_0^2e^u\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\\\\n&=\\sqrt2[e^u]_0^2\\\\\n&=\\sqrt2(e^2-1).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20dd3aaa-0c4c-5e48-9b30-f0423a7f2865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708886} {:answer/id #uuid "263d0601-ef45-56e9-91ee-f90fd9ede404" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708887} {:answer/id #uuid "604151c1-72fc-56fc-bb4a-9227d7b341ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708892} {:answer/id #uuid "7bee63ee-0e1b-5a33-955b-4d5b1ad21bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708894} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f8dd12-a351-5549-a1d2-1269c3b51127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708897}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708897} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbf36928-3c3e-5313-a9ef-c00bb231027f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e47f518c-f1fd-5945-8067-a46f28547671" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int_C (x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s$, where $C$ is the line segment from $(2,1)$ to $(0,1)$." :question/worked-solution "Use the scalar line-integral formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor $\\mathbf a=(2,1)$ and $\\mathbf b=(0,1)$, parameterize the segment by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\mathbf a+t(\\mathbf b-\\mathbf a)=(2-2t,1),\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\n$$\n\nThis gives the stated starting point at $t=0$ and ending point at $t=1$. Thus $x=2-2t$ and $y=1$. The derivative and speed are\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r'(t)=(-2,0),\\qquad \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|=\\sqrt{(-2)^2+0^2}=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the function gives $f(\\mathbf r(t))=(2-2t)+1=3-2t$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C (x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n&=2\\int_0^1(3-2t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=2[3t-t^2]_0^1\\\\\n&=2(3-1)=4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe speed is positive even though $x$ decreases. Reversing the direction does not change an integral with respect to arc length."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02618be7-d5d2-5f29-9afd-fd2da49f9894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708937} {:answer/id #uuid "2ba56b80-2f8d-51cf-bd8c-009011293d32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708941} {:answer/id #uuid "2e2be7eb-78bf-564f-a5bf-9d363bffaa64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708942} {:answer/id #uuid "51cd5e3e-e390-52de-b9c4-f9cdc66dca7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708946} {:answer/id #uuid "ee01004f-2813-5638-9a62-4722b96bbb21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708968}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708968} :answer-field/id #uuid "9da432e4-a599-537c-9f64-ca8a41569fb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "038e1e3e-68cb-508f-88ba-a4d861b1600d" :question/problem "![](images/0e/0e4a78829ce8d1135d46dda1db59c968c0306937d9c5a45b24fa41648a679ea4.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a line segment from the point $O(0,0)$ to the point $A(2,0),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(2,0)$ to the point $B(1,1).$\n\nTraverse $C=C_1\\cup C_2$ in the stated order. Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=(2 x)\\mathbf i+(- x + 2 y)\\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nGiven that\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=4,\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$." :question/worked-solution "Use additivity over the two oriented pieces.\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n$$\n\nThe contribution from $C_1$ is supplied, so calculate $C_2$ only. Choose $x=2 - t$ and $y=t$, with $t$ running from $0$ to $1$ in that order. The endpoint substitutions give the start and end of the stated piece.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_2(t)&=(2 - t)\\mathbf i+(t)\\mathbf j, \\\\ \\mathbf r_2'(t)&=(-1)\\mathbf i+(1)\\mathbf j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mathbf r_2(t))&=4 - 2 t, \\\\ Q(\\mathbf r_2(t))&=3 t - 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nForm the dot product, keeping both tangent factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r_2(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r_2'(t)&=(4 - 2 t)(-1) \\\\ &\\quad+(3 t - 2)(1) \\\\ &=5 t - 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate in the specified direction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_{0}^{1}(5 t - 6)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[\\frac{5 t^{2}}{2} - 6 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=- \\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the supplied contribution:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=(4)+\\left(- \\frac{7}{2}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708940 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39009434-cb05-500a-94d1-954042a446b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708944} {:answer/id #uuid "659c8468-9b92-52ed-a7bc-65968cf352eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708952} {:answer/id #uuid "66ec9439-08fa-584e-8124-4b8826876129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708953} {:answer/id #uuid "d531407b-c81f-5fb2-a011-fe6991a8e230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708962} {:answer/id #uuid "fc5a06e9-35dc-5fd7-a692-84b3fc8dcd3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708970}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708970} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb0e4318-48a7-5bfd-b3a9-4fdc3c6aa411" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1d3bde2c-54cc-563a-a46b-36e16c73a1ae" :question/problem "![](images/60/6087da076e65bda5240c428ff67c570ad59ae9a8e5a5a3c9e8406184998de56a.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a the line segment from the point $O(0,0)$ to the point $A(1,0),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(1,0)$ to the point $B(0,-2).$\n\nTraverse $C=C_1\\cup C_2$ in the stated order. Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=(2 x - 2 y)\\mathbf i+(- x)\\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nGiven that\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=1,\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$." :question/worked-solution "Use additivity over the two oriented pieces.\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n$$\n\nThe contribution from $C_1$ is supplied, so calculate $C_2$ only. Choose $x=1 - t$ and $y=- 2 t$, with $t$ running from $0$ to $1$ in that order. The endpoint substitutions give the start and end of the stated piece.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_2(t)&=(1 - t)\\mathbf i+(- 2 t)\\mathbf j, \\\\ \\mathbf r_2'(t)&=(-1)\\mathbf i+(-2)\\mathbf j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mathbf r_2(t))&=2 t + 2, \\\\ Q(\\mathbf r_2(t))&=t - 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nForm the dot product, keeping both tangent factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r_2(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r_2'(t)&=(2 t + 2)(-1) \\\\ &\\quad+(t - 1)(-2) \\\\ &=- 4 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate in the specified direction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_{0}^{1}(- 4 t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[- 2 t^{2}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the supplied contribution:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=(1)+(-2)=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708956 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d6b2795-d1b0-560b-b85f-2b912a6794e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708939} {:answer/id #uuid "4b242d05-db62-5371-a038-30830d261f32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708945} {:answer/id #uuid "5f5dceab-7a77-57c7-949d-b49dbe22f197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708949} {:answer/id #uuid "94b79f65-7247-58f4-8e4a-a486b101b7a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708958} {:answer/id #uuid "de3a10c5-c5b9-54f0-aa0f-8d964b142662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708963}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708963} :answer-field/id #uuid "e015a860-88f9-57f6-8769-be10d413e727" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "80444472-cb79-5122-b9eb-cc42e46fed63" :question/problem "![](images/04/0457cb819e6f39ef9c0978e356cff788e1cf5edbef9cbf844a054ab777b70eac.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a the line segment from the point $A(-2,0)$ to the point $B(0,1),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of the line segment from the point $B(0,1)$ to the point $D(1,1).$\n\nTraverse $C=C_1\\cup C_2$ in the stated order. Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=(x + 2 y)\\mathbf i+(- y)\\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nGiven that\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\frac{5}{2},\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$." :question/worked-solution "Use additivity over the two oriented pieces.\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n$$\n\nThe contribution from $C_2$ is supplied, so calculate $C_1$ only. Choose $x=2 t - 2$ and $y=t$, with $t$ running from $0$ to $1$ in that order. The endpoint substitutions give the start and end of the stated piece.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_1(t)&=(2 t - 2)\\mathbf i+(t)\\mathbf j, \\\\ \\mathbf r_1'(t)&=(2)\\mathbf i+(1)\\mathbf j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mathbf r_1(t))&=4 t - 2, \\\\ Q(\\mathbf r_1(t))&=- t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nForm the dot product, keeping both tangent factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r_1(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r_1'(t)&=(4 t - 2)(2) \\\\ &\\quad+(- t)(1) \\\\ &=7 t - 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate in the specified direction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_{0}^{1}(7 t - 4)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[\\frac{7 t^{2}}{2} - 4 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the supplied contribution:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708960 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3147d2db-46d5-5700-b265-0f3f09d0fb98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708943} {:answer/id #uuid "5d4f8bde-5c91-52de-ba42-fafbfdf6765a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708948} {:answer/id #uuid "77cb7ef5-703d-51d8-8b88-ebe94deb97c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708954} {:answer/id #uuid "855d2103-7614-5b39-ae8c-3410b603f83a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708957} {:answer/id #uuid "f87a3a16-6967-5d64-a828-c1c6bb5e8d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708969}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708969} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5cf0451-77ed-5ad1-b98f-d410ead56c0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9e8d2f75-989e-5b17-981b-1f4699b960ed" :question/problem "![](images/73/73c6a8268a179f72611fb65e099d1249d48501e4fd4731d03747800e1944fd97.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a the line segment from the point $A(0,1)$ to the point $B(1,2),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $B(1,2)$ to the point $D(1,3).$\n\nTraverse $C=C_1\\cup C_2$ in the stated order. Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=(0)\\mathbf i+(- 2 x + y)\\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nGiven that\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$." :question/worked-solution "Use additivity over the two oriented pieces.\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n$$\n\nThe contribution from $C_2$ is supplied, so calculate $C_1$ only. Choose $x=t$ and $y=t + 1$, with $t$ running from $0$ to $1$ in that order. The endpoint substitutions give the start and end of the stated piece.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_1(t)&=(t)\\mathbf i+(t + 1)\\mathbf j, \\\\ \\mathbf r_1'(t)&=(1)\\mathbf i+(1)\\mathbf j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mathbf r_1(t))&=0, \\\\ Q(\\mathbf r_1(t))&=1 - t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nForm the dot product, keeping both tangent factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r_1(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r_1'(t)&=(0)(1) \\\\ &\\quad+(1 - t)(1) \\\\ &=1 - t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate in the specified direction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_{0}^{1}(1 - t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[- \\frac{t^{2}}{2} + t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the supplied contribution:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=1.\n$$"}]}
